# TURNING ONE PIXEL ON, AND OFF.
#
#   python3 -m sparkblocks run t1-one-pixel.spark
#
# `screen 8 4` makes a grid 8 across and 4 down.
# `light 3 1` turns on the pixel at column 3, row 1 -- when the
# number coming down the chain is over the line (0.5 by default).
#
# Try: change `const 1` to `const 0` and it goes off instead.

screen 8 4
const 1
light 3 1
draw
